1. Introduction to Flexbox
Flexbox is a one-dimensional layout system used to arrange items in rows or columns.
It helps distribute space and align items efficiently.
Example:
<div class="container">
  <div>Item 1</div>
  <div>Item 2</div>
</div>

<style>
.container {
  display: flex;
}
</style>


2. Flex Container Setup
You enable flexbox using display:flex. This turns the container into a flex container.
Example:
<div class="container">
  <div>Box</div>
</div>

<style>
.container {
  display: flex;
}
</style>


3. flex-direction
Controls the direction of items (row, column, etc).
Example:
<div class="container">
  <div>1</div>
  <div>2</div>
</div>

<style>
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}
</style>


4. justify-content
Aligns items along the main axis.
Example:
<div class="container">
  <div>1</div>
  <div>2</div>
</div>

<style>
.container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
}
</style>


5. align-items
Aligns items along the cross axis.
Example:
<div class="container">
  <div>1</div>
  <div>2</div>
</div>

<style>
.container {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  height: 200px;
}
</style>


6. flex-wrap
Controls whether items wrap to the next line.
Example:
<div class="container">
  <div>1</div>
  <div>2</div>
  <div>3</div>
</div>

<style>
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
</style>


7. gap
Adds spacing between flex items.
Example:
<div class="container">
  <div>1</div>
  <div>2</div>
</div>

<style>
.container {
  display: flex;
  gap: 20px;
}
</style>


8. flex-grow
Defines how much an item should grow relative to others.
Example:
<div class="container">
  <div class="a">1</div>
  <div class="b">2</div>
</div>

<style>
.container { display: flex; }
.a { flex-grow: 1; }
.b { flex-grow: 2; }
</style>


9. flex-shrink
Defines how items shrink when space is limited.
Example:
<style>
.container { display: flex; }
.item { flex-shrink: 1; }
</style>


10. flex-basis
Sets the initial size before space distribution.
Example:
<style>
.container { display: flex; }
.item { flex-basis: 200px; }
</style>


11. flex shorthand
Combines grow, shrink, and basis.
Example:
<style>
.item {
  flex: 1;
}
</style>


12. align-self
Overrides alignment for a single item.
Example:
<style>
.item {
  align-self: flex-end;
}
</style>


13. order
Changes the visual order of items.
Example:
<style>
.item1 { order: 2; }
.item2 { order: 1; }
</style>


